{"type":"text","timestamp":1794305692784,"sessionID":"ses_e3b11e6dfffeWcbapUoSOODIDW","part":{"id":"prt_1c4f4144e001u7t5Urc6RyBwK5","messageID":"msg_1c4f3fb98001BxZl2pgEYKUEkl","sessionID":"ses_e3b11e6dfffeWcbapUoSOODIDW","type":"text","text":"The book library app is complete. Here's what I built:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`) — Flask + SQLite under `./data`:\n- Auth via bearer tokens (`register` 201, `login` → `{token}`), hashed passwords\n- Full CRUD: books (paged list with `q`/`page`/`page_size`, create, get, PUT with year/isbn clearing, delete cascading reviews) and reviews (list, create with once-per-user enforcement)\n- `average_rating` computed and rounded to one decimal, `null` without reviews\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`) — React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`), react-router:\n- Sign-in/register forms, header showing username + sign-out\n- Book table with search + paging, star ratings\n- Book detail page with reviews, rating form (signed-in), edit/delete (delete confirms)\n- Add/edit forms surfacing API validation messages\n\n**Verified**: unit-style tests against the Flask test client (auth, validation, review dedupe, PUT clearing, cascade delete) all pass; the frontend builds cleanly; the app boots under gunicorn and serves `/api/health`, the SPA, and API end-to-end.\n\nOne note: `docker` isn't installed in this sandbox, so I couldn't build the image itself, but I confirmed the app runs correctly with the exact gunicorn command the Dockerfile uses.","time":{"start":1794305692750,"end":1794305692754}}}
